   "mechanism": "IL12B acts as part of the IL-23 cytokine, which binds to the IL23R receptor complex. This interaction activates TYK2, propagating signals that induce Th17 cell commitment and IL-17 secretion. IL-17 in turn activates TRAF3IP2 within skin cells, causing the runaway inflammation seen in psoriasis. Each node is supported by strong genetic associations and validated therapeutic interventions.",
